### Variables — edit these for your environment
### Signs in as a regular realm user (password grant through the realm's public admin-cli client).
### The user needs realm-management roles (or fine-grained admin permissions) to view organizations and users.
@keycloak-host = {{$processEnv Keycloak__BaseUrl}}
@realm = my-personal-archive
@client-id = admin-cli
@username = arjan@einbu.no
@org-alias = winge-einbu-family


### 1. Get a user token (password grant from admin-cli in the realm)
# @name getUserToken
# @prompt password Password for the user
POST {{keycloak-host}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id={{client-id}}&username={{username}}&password={{password}}&grant_type=password


### 2. Find the organization by name/alias
# @name findOrg
GET {{keycloak-host}}/admin/realms/{{realm}}/organizations
Authorization: Bearer {{getUserToken.response.body.access_token}}
Accept: application/json


### 3. List members of the organization
GET {{keycloak-host}}/admin/realms/{{realm}}/organizations/{{findOrg.response.body.0.id}}/members?briefRepresentation=false
Authorization: Bearer {{getUserToken.response.body.access_token}}
Accept: application/json
